<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alutiiq</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sugpiaq</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alutiiq, or Sugpiaq, are an Indigenous people of south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a>, living on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kodiak-island">Kodiak Island</a>, the Alaska Peninsula and the coasts of Prince William Sound. In 1784 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grigory-shelikhov">Grigory Shelikhov</a>'s men massacred many of them at Refuge Rock, and under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-american-company">Russian-American Company</a> they were forced to hunt sea otters.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alutiiq.jpg" alt="Alutiiq" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christopher Mertl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AlutiiqDancer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
